STRING 1222
{
Anya
}

STRING 1223
{
There’s a Dark Ranger camp ahead. Let’s check in with them first.
}

STRING 1224
{
Faranell
}

STRING 1225
{
Anya, we’ve been expecting you. Putress sent us the list of reagents he requires.
}

STRING 1226
{
Anya
}

STRING 1227
{
How thoughtful of him. I trust things are going well here?
}

STRING 1230
{
Faranell
}

STRING 1231
{
Well enough. Though I do long for the comforts of my laboratory.
}

STRING 1232
{
Melisara
}

STRING 1233
{
That idiot Gordo has gone missing again, Anya. Drag him back to camp if you find him, will you?
}

STRING 1234
{
Anya
}

STRING 1235
{
We’ll keep our eyes open. Dark Lady watch over you.
}

STRING 1236
{
Garek
}

STRING 1237
{
Anya, how did I end up in Putress’s apothecarium to begin with?
}

STRING 1238
{
Anya
}

STRING 1239
{
You were among the Scourge forces that held the Capital City when Lady Sylvanas came to claim it.
}

STRING 1240
{
Anya
}

STRING 1241
{
After the battle, we gathered the remaining undead and sent them to Putress for... processing.
}

STRING 1242
{
Garek
}

STRING 1243
{
So I fought against Sylvanas when I was in the Scourge? And yet she welcomes me as one of the Forsaken?
}

STRING 1244
{
Anya
}

STRING 1245
{
She understands all too well what it means to be forced to do the Lich King’s bidding.
}

STRING 1246
{
Anya
}

STRING 1247
{
How could she turn away a newly awakened Forsaken, no matter what they had done before?
}

STRING 1248
{
Garek
}

STRING 1249
{
What about you, Anya? How did you join the Forsaken?
}

STRING 1250
{
Anya
}

STRING 1251
{
In life, I served under Sylvanas. We both died defending our kingdom against the Scourge. And we were both raised into undeath.
}

STRING 1252
{
Anya
}

STRING 1253
{
When I regained my free will, the Dark Lady offered me a place to belong. And for that, she has my eternal loyalty.
}

STRING 1254
{
Garek
}

STRING 1255
{
Do you remember what you were forced to do when you were under the Lich King’s control?
}

STRING 1256
{
Anya
}

STRING 1257
{
Yes. But I will not discuss it, Garek. Not with you, nor with anyone else.
}

STRING 1258
{
Anya
}

STRING 1259
{
Reliving the past will not change it. Better to move forward without looking back.
}

STRING 1260
{
Garek
}

STRING 1261
{
It seems many of the Forsaken have stories like yours. Cursed with undeath, seeking to make the most of a grim fate.
}

STRING 1262
{
Anya
}

STRING 1263
{
We are indeed united by our torment. The world sees us as monsters, and so we have only eachother to rely upon.
}

STRING 1266
{
Garek
}

STRING 1267
{
Then I will endeavor to be reliable. For Lady Sylvanas, and for the Forsaken.
}

STRING 1270
{
Glix
}

STRING 1271
{
Hey! We could use some help here! We’d make it worth your while!
}

STRING 1272
{
Anya
}

STRING 1273
{
Hmm. Go on.
}

STRING 1274
{
Glix
}

STRING 1275
{
We got ambushed by gnolls and had to abandon our inventory. If you get it back for us, we’ll give you a quarter of our stock.
}

STRING 1276
{
Anya
}

STRING 1277
{
Make it half or we walk away.
}

STRING 1278
{
Glix
}

STRING 1279
{
Half?! That’s highway robbery!
}

STRING 1280
{
Glix
}

STRING 1281
{
Well... we have already been robbed once today. All right, deal.
}

STRING 1288
{
Glix
}

STRING 1289
{
The gnoll camp is to the south of here. Don’t die! Again.
}

STRING 1290
{
Glix
}

STRING 1291
{
Hey, you did it! And our merchandise is still intact!
}

STRING 1292
{
Anya
}

STRING 1293
{
Indeed. Now, about our payment.
}

STRING 1294
{
Glix
}

STRING 1295
{
Of course! We’d be glad to personally transport your half of the supplies to your, uh, Undercity, was it?
}

STRING 1296
{
Glix
}

STRING 1297
{
What better way to show our appreciation to our new customers-- I mean-- gracious hosts?
}

STRING 1298
{
Anya
}

STRING 1299
{
You sneaky little--
}

STRING 1300
{
Garek
}

STRING 1301
{
Which we graciously accept. The Forsaken will benefit from your wares. See you in the city.
}

STRING 1302
{
Garek
}

STRING 1303
{
The Forsaken need supplies, which the goblins can provide. And if they’re reliant on the Undercity for protection...
}

STRING 1304
{
Anya
}

STRING 1305
{
We’re simply going to let them set up shop in the Undercity?
}

STRING 1306
{
Garek
}

STRING 1307
{
Then the Dark Lady can negotiate their prices from a position of strength. Impressive, Bandaron.
}

STRING 1310
{
Anya
}

STRING 1311
{
As one of the Forsaken, you may develop an affinity for spiders. But it would still be wise to approach them with caution.
}

STRING 1314
{
Gordo
}

STRING 1315
{
Sticky webs! Gordo needs help!
}

STRING 1316
{
Anya
}

STRING 1317
{
Yet another fine mess, Gordo!
}

STRING 1318
{
Gordo
}

STRING 1319
{
Gordo free! Going back to camp now!
}

STRING 1320
{
Anya
}

STRING 1321
{
Try not to wander off again.
}

STRING 1322
{
Garek
}

STRING 1323
{
A vile sickness festers throughout these woods.
}

STRING 1324
{
Anya
}

STRING 1325
{
The Scourge’s handiwork. They sought to blight all of Lordaeron.
}

STRING 1326
{
Anya
}

STRING 1327
{
Now this land belongs to the Forsaken. We suffer neither the Scourge nor the living to intrude.
}

STRING 1328
{
Anya
}

STRING 1329
{
Murlocs. Foul creatures, but their scales are useful in alchemy.
}

STRING 1330
{
Anya
}

STRING 1331
{
That’s everything Putress wants. Let’s head back to the Undercity.
}

STRING 1332
{
Melisara
}

STRING 1333
{
Gordo collected a few goods while he was wandering out there. They might be worth a look.
}

STRING 1336
{
Anya
}

STRING 1337
{
The quarry is on the northern edge of the woods. Let’s move.
}

STRING 1338
{
Garek
}

STRING 1339
{
One might say that there is value to be found in our former lives after all.
}

STRING 1340
{
Garek
}

STRING 1341
{
It’s fortunate that Bernd remembers masonry from when he was alive. His skills will benefit the Undercity.
}

STRING 1342
{
Anya
}

STRING 1343
{
Hmph. You speak quite knowingly about such things, for one who awakened so recently.
}

STRING 1344
{
Garek
}

STRING 1345
{
Yes, well. It’s like you said. I do catch on quickly, don’t I?
}

STRING 1346
{
Garek
}

STRING 1347
{
Looks like the ogres have set up some fortifications
}

STRING 1350
{
Anya
}

STRING 1351
{
Then we have a choice to make. Either we attack head on, or we look for another way in.
}

STRING 1354
{
Garek
}

STRING 1355
{
It’s good to know that this quarry will supply Bernd’s workforce.
}

STRING 1356
{
Anya
}

STRING 1357
{
With their leader slain, the rest of the ogres will scatter into the hills.
}

STRING 1358
{
Herszt bandytów
}

STRING 1359
{
The undead! Cut them apart and take their valuables!
}

STRING 1362
{
Anya
}

STRING 1363
{
Well, these look like the parts Keever asked us to collect.
}

STRING 1364
{
Anya
}

STRING 1365
{
That ghoul appears to be fishing. I’ve never seen that before.
}

STRING 1366
{
Garek
}

STRING 1367
{
Quickly, after them!
}

